{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788328067807300001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"earthen-wheat-chick","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"ef1a1608c058fff9523f0882b40e957282b7822784a695d37426cb7c70f8725a","event_uuid":"6780c5ff-88c3-4e74-bf4e-e5e1056263cd","position":{"commit_sha":"819015f2e6149f820fd70de046d3ad96f3f0826a","position":"1788314634890101001-6780c5ff-88c3-4e74-bf4e-e5e1056263cd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d6eea4f7eff90fbc66784ba31a1bcd17a5d3e30a24eddc15712718e7f6a8850f","event_uuid":"f01cf245-01d9-45ae-bf0c-4e3c6687b0f8","position":{"commit_sha":"dab8efcb380d81e38b9677bc2903389c74406cfe","position":"1788314661029444001-f01cf245-01d9-45ae-bf0c-4e3c6687b0f8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788314634890101001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`docs/api-stability.md:24,41-46` defines underscore-prefixed modules/functions as private, while ADR 0083 already requires one canonical binding for reconciler moves. Contrary decisions remain: ADR 0016 retains `run_security_detectors`, ADR 0092 retains reconcile compatibility, and past split documentation retained private shims to avoid consumer migration.\n\n## Approach\n\nComplete the prescribed ADR lifecycle. In RESEARCH, catalog the cited contrary decisions and write a numbered critique covering public-versus-private boundaries, dynamic/monkeypatch consumers, persisted/wire exceptions, and enforcement. Record maintainer resolution for every critique item. Then DRAFT, HOLD for review, and MERGE an ADR that mandates one canonical private binding and atomic consumer migration.\n\n## Scope\n\n- new ADR allocated through `docs/adr/.numbers`\n- `docs/api-stability.md` and architecture/reuse guidance\n- enforcement/review guidance or a mechanical guard identified by the ADR\n\n## Testing\n\nAdd a policy/documentation check or deterministic enforcement test specified by the ADR; verify existing public facade, wire-schema, and persisted-event contract tests remain unaffected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] RESEARCH contains a numbered critique of ADR 0016, ADR 0083, ADR 0092, and prior split-shim guidance; each item has a recorded maintainer resolution.\n- [ ] The merged ADR defines one canonical binding after private moves and atomic source/test/string/dynamic/monkeypatch migration.\n- [ ] The ADR distinguishes valid public facades, MCP wire schemas, event readers, and persisted-data migrations from internal-only shims.\n- [ ] The ADR requires a durable review or mechanical recurrence-prevention mechanism and names its evidence.\n- [ ] The policy check/enforcement evidence passes without breaking the preserved public/wire/event contracts.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers","reason":"allocate the next ADR number through the established mechanism"},{"path":"docs/adr","reason":"add the governing no-internal-shim ADR"},{"path":"docs/api-stability.md","reason":"align private/public compatibility guidance"},{"path":"docs/architecture.md","reason":"align internal move/re-export guidance"},{"path":"tests","reason":"add or update policy/enforcement evidence required by ADR"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","6640-ac11-5c55-46b5"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"6640-ac11-5c55-46b5","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["janitor","adr","architecture","internal-shims"],"ticket_id":"8eff-87c1-d09a-4893","ticket_type":"task","title":"ADR: prohibit internal-only compatibility shims","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6780c5ff-88c3-4e74-bf4e-e5e1056263cd","f01cf245-01d9-45ae-bf0c-4e3c6687b0f8"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788328067807300001,"uuid":"2312699b-3c02-4daf-9653-58bef91ba32b"}